# ===========================================================================
# AntiHide V2 - Git ignore rules
#
# Scope: this is a single-module Android/Kotlin project. The rules below are
# deliberately narrow. Nothing here blocks Markdown, scripts, tests, JSON,
# resources or verification evidence from being tracked.
#
# Verify what a rule affects with:   git check-ignore -v <path>
# ===========================================================================

# --- Gradle ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Project-local Gradle state: caches, file hashes, execution history, VCS
# metadata. Machine-local and fully regenerated by the next build.
.gradle/

# Build output: compiled classes, dex, intermediates, incremental caches,
# the generated test reports and the assembled APK. All reproducible from
# source with a single command; none of it is reviewable.
build/
app/build/

# Gradle wrapper JAR is intentionally NOT ignored - it is required for anyone
# to build. Only the local unpacked distribution is disposable.
!gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar

# --- Android local configuration -------------------------------------------
# Contains sdk.dir=C:\Users\<username>\... : an absolute path that reveals the
# operator's Windows account name and is specific to one machine.
# Android Studio writes this automatically; it is not part of the project.
local.properties

# --- Signing material -----------------------------------------------------
# No keystore is committed and none should ever be. Keep the whole class of
# release-signing material out of version control.
*.jks
*.keystore
*.p12
*.pfx
keystore.properties
signing.properties

# --- Secrets and environment ----------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
secrets.properties

# --- IDE and editor state -------------------------------------------------
.idea/
*.iml
.kotlin/
.classpath
.project
.settings/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo

# --- Browser automation tooling output -------------------------------------
# Browser-console captures from manual real-device dashboard verification.
# These are scratch output, not evidence, and they can capture the machine's
# own tailnet hostnames and addresses. The curated result of that manual
# verification is recorded in docs/VERIFICATION.md instead.
.playwright-mcp/

# --- AI coding-agent local state -------------------------------------------
# Sessions, caches, conversation exports and scratch state written by AI coding
# assistants and MCP servers. None of this is product, and none of it should
# ever reach the published repository.
#
# NOTE: AGENTS.md and CLAUDE.md are deliberately NOT listed here. Unlike the
# .local.md variants below, a committed AGENTS.md or CLAUDE.md is legitimate
# contributor guidance and is worth tracking. Only the per-machine overrides
# are ignored.
.opencode/
.claude/
.agents/
.agent/
.codex/
.cursor/
.aider/
.continue/
.windsurf/
.gemini/
.roo/

# Per-machine instruction overrides (by definition not shareable).
AGENTS.local.md
CLAUDE.local.md
CLAUDE.md.local

# Agent / MCP tool configuration, which is personal machine setup.
.mcp.json
mcp.json
opencode.json
opencode.jsonc

# Agent scratch space, session dumps and local diagnostic output. Anchored to
# the repository root so a legitimately-named directory deeper in the tree is
# never swallowed by accident.
/.tmp/
/tmp/
/.cache/
/logs/
/.scratch/
/scratch/

# Additional browser-automation output directories (the MCP one is above).
/.playwright/
/playwright-report/
/blob-report/
/.playwright-artifacts/

# --- Repository-preparation working documents (local only) -------------------
# These are point-in-time working audits produced while preparing this
# repository. They are machine-generated process records, not product
# documentation: every finding in them has since been resolved, and the durable
# conclusions live in README.md and docs/.
#
# GITHUB_READINESS_REPORT.md additionally contains the operator's real Tailscale
# addresses, MagicDNS hostname, tailnet name and Windows account name. It must
# never be published. It is kept on disk as a local working document only.
#
# To publish a redacted security summary instead, write a concise hand-authored
# SECURITY.md and add a negation for it below.
GITHUB_READINESS_REPORT.md
GITHUB_RELEASE_PREPARATION_REPORT.md
CODING_AGENT_ARTIFACT_CLEANUP_REPORT.md
FINAL_RELEASE_FILE_AUDIT.md
*_REPORT.md
!SECURITY.md

# --- Logs, temp files and OS metadata --------------------------------------
*.log
*.tmp
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# ===========================================================================
# DELIBERATE NON-EXCLUSIONS
#
# The following are intentionally NOT ignored and should be committed:
#
#   gradle/wrapper/        Required to build. The wrapper JAR must be tracked.
#   scripts/*.ps1          The real-device verification harnesses are part of
#                          the project's value, not disposable tooling.
#   app/src/**             All production source, assets and the JUnit suite.
#   docs/*.md              Curated, sanitized verification evidence.
#   README.md              Project documentation.
#   app/src/main/res/raw/  The alarm tone is a source asset, not an artifact.
#   AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md   IF these are ever added as committed contributor
#                          guidance, track them. Only the .local.md per-machine
#                          overrides above are ignored.
#
# There is deliberately no blanket *.apk rule. The build-output APK is already
# excluded by app/build/. A future signed release APK should be published as a
# GitHub Release asset rather than committed, so no APK belongs in the
# repository at all.
#
# There is deliberately no blanket ignore for directories named scripts/, docs/,
# config/ or tests/. Those names are load-bearing in this repository and must
# stay trackable.
# ===========================================================================
